    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d532">

                <pb facs="0714" n="428" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg428"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/2810</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Guayaquil</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Goding</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Guayaquil</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-08-09T15:00:00-05:14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 9, 1916, 3 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 9.20 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have been notified, by Grace and Company all their steamers refuse to carry
                    cargo belonging black-list Americans as well as others to any port. Shall I
                    refuse bills health?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Goding</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
